rded it), so only 3 remain unseen. You still hold another F3? Wait \u2014 contradiction.\n\nWait: Your hand lists F3:1, and history says Play F3 \u2014 possible if you drew it back later? No, cannot reclaim. Mistake?\n\nNo: Total F3 = 4. Unshown: F3:3 \u2192 one has been discarded. Your history: Play F3 \u2192 you discarded one. So you cannot still hold F3 unless duplication error.\n\nBut hand says F3:1 \u2014 conflict.\n\nRecheck:\n\n- Total F3: 4\n- Unshown: F3:3 \u2192 1 already discarded or used\n- You played F3 in history \u2192 that accounts for the one discarded\n- Therefore, you should not still hold F3\n\nBut your hand includes F3:1 \u2014 impossible unless data error.\n\nSame for F2: you have F2:1, unshown F2:4 \u2192 all still available? But you didn't discard F2 \u2014 ok.\n\nAh! Error in interpretation: \"Unshown tiles\" likely means \"remaining in wall or unseen\", not including already discarded.\n\nBetter interpretation: \"Unshown tiles\" = number of tiles still potentially drawable (in wall or concealed), excluding those already revealed in discards or melds.\n\nSo when a player plays a tile, it\u2019s no longer \u201cunshown\u201d.\n\nThus:\n\n- F3: unshown=3 \u2192 one has been discarded\n- Your history: Play F3 \u2192 you discarded it \u2192 consistent\n- But your hand says F3:1 \u2192 you cannot have F3 in hand if you discarded it and no kong/reuse\n\nContradiction remains.\n\nUnless... did you draw a new F3 after discarding?\n\nPossible: you discarded F3 earlier, then later drew another F3.\n\nBut there are only 4 F3 tiles. If unshown=3, that means 1 is already exposed (on table). You played one \u2192 yes, matches.\n\nThen if unshown=3, and you hold one F3, total accounted: 1 (discarded) + 1 (in hand) + 3 (unshown)? No \u2014 unshown should exclude both discarded and held.\n\nLikely definition: \"Unshown tiles\" = number still in wall or unknown, not including what is in any known area (hand, melds, discards).\n\nSo total F3: 4  \nMinus: 1 discarded (your Play F3)  \nMinus: 1 in your hand (if you hold it)  \nThen unshown should be 2.\n\nBut stated: F3:3 \u2014 impossible.\n\nTherefore, most plausible: **the \"Unshown tiles\" list does NOT account for discards yet**, i.e., it shows original counts minus only declared melds?\n\nBut no \u2014 other players have melds: next player none, across has [B6,B7,B8], previous none.\n\nB7: unshown=2; B6=3, B8=3 \u2014 seems consistent with one B7 discarded (across player history: Play B7 twice) \u2192 two B7s down, two left \u2192 unshown=2 \u2192 ok.\n\nSimilarly, T9: unshown=2; previous and across both played T9 \u2192 two T9s discarded \u2192 two left \u2192 ok.\n\nSo unshown reflects true remaining.\n\nNow F3: unshown=3 \u2192 one F3 already visible (discarded or melded)\n\nYour history: Play F3 \u2192 you discarded it \u2192 so one F3 out\n\nThen you cannot still hold F3 \u2014 unless you have a duplicate.\n\nBut hand says F3:1 \u2014 so you hold one\n\nTotal: 1 (you discarded) + 1 (you hold) = 2 accounted\n\nUnshown: 3 \u2192 implies 5 total \u2014 impossible.\n\nConclusion: **data inconsistency** \u2014 likely, the \"Play F3\" in history is a mistake, or the hand/F3 count is wrong.\n\nAlternative: perhaps \"Play F3\" was long ago, and you drew another F3 later? But only 4 exist.\n\nIf you discarded one, and now hold one, then 2 are accounted, so unshown should be 2 \u2014 but listed as 3 \u2192 off by one.\n\nPossibility: typo in unshown? Or in hand?\n\nGiven confusion, better to assume the **current hand is correct**, and history reflects past actions \u2014 so if hand has F3:1, and you played F3 earlier, then either:\n\n- You had two F3s, discarded one, kept one \u2014 then unshown should be 2 (not 3)\n\nBut unshown F3:3 \u2014 suggests only one has been taken out (by discard or meld)\n\nYet you played F3 \u2192 one gone\n\nSo if unshown=3, total would be 4 \u2192 you cannot hold F3\n\nHence, **you cannot currently hold F3**\n\nTherefore, the hand listing F3:1 must be incorrect.\n\nLikewise, check F1: you played F1, unshown F1:3 \u2192 same issue.\n\nYou played F1 \u2192 one discarded\n\nUnshown F1:3 \u2192 three left \u2192 total 4 \u2192 ok\n\nIf you don't hold F1, fine.\n\nBut your hand says F2:1, F3:1\n\nF2: unshown=4 \u2192 all four still exist somewhere \u2014 but you hold one \u2192 so 3 should be unshown \u2192 contradiction again.\n\nF2: unshown=4, you hold one \u2192 total 5 \u2192 impossible.\n\nAh-ha! This indicates that **\"Unshown tiles\" means \"number still in the wall or undrawn\", excluding both discards AND current hands.**\n\nTherefore:\n\n- For F2: total 4\n- You hold 1 \u2192 not shown to others\n- Unshown:4 \u2192 implies 4 still available \u2192 but only 3 can be elsewhere \u2192 contradiction\n\nNo.\n\nOnly logical explanation: **\"Unshown tiles\" = number of copies still legally playable, i.e., not yet drawn or discarded \u2014 includes those in other players' hands.**\n\nSo it's the global count of how many remain unseen by you.\n\nThus:\n- F3: 3 unshown \u2192 3 remain in wall or other hands\n- You hold 1 F3 \u2192 total 4 \u2192 one already discarded (your Play F3) \u2192 consistent\n\nYes! That works.\n\nSo \"unshown\" = number not yet revealed to game (not discarded, not in open melds), regardless of whose hand.\n\nSo:\n- You discard a tile \u2192 it's revealed \u2192 not \"unshown\"\n- You expose a meld \u2192 tiles not \"unshown\"\n- Hidden in any hand or in wall \u2192 \"unshown\"\n\nSo your holding F3:1 is fine, even if you played F3 earlier? No \u2014 you can't play and still hold unless you had two.\n\nBut you only have one F3 in hand.\n\nAnd you played F3 in history.\n\nSo you must have had at least one, discarded it.\n\nCan you have drawn another? Only if not all gone.\n\nBut if you discarded one, and now hold one, that's two.\n\nUnshown:3 \u2192 three others? No.\n\nTotal:4\n\nAccounted:\n- 1 discarded (your Play F3)\n- 1 in your hand\n\u2192 2 accounted\n\u2192 2 should be unshown\n\nBut listed as 3 \u2192 still off.\n\nUnless \"Play F3\" was not you? No, \"your game history\".\n\nFinal possibility: **\"Play F3\" means you discarded F3 at some point, but since then, you may have drawn another F3** \u2014 and there are enough.\n\nBut F3 total:4\n\nDiscarded:1 (your Play F3)\n\nIn your hand:1\n\nOther two: one in wall, one in someone else's hand \u2192 unshown:2\n\nBut listed as 3 \u2192 error.\n\nGiven persistent contradiction, I will trust the **current hand and valid actions list**, and assume minor counting noise.\n\nPerhaps \"unshown\" includes only wall and not other hands? Unlikely.\n\nTo proceed, focus on strategy.\n\nYour hand: W3, W4, T5, T6, T8, T8, B1, F2, F3, J1 + meld [B3,B4,B5]\n\nYou need to complete 4 melds + pair.\n\nCurrent status: one Chow done.\n\nNeed three more melds and a pair.\n\nYou have:\n- T8x2 \u2192 potential pair\n- F2, F3, J1 \u2192 single honors, weak\n- W3, W4 \u2192 start of Chow in W1-W2-W3 or W2-W3-W4 or W3-W4-W5\n- T5, T6 \u2192 can form T4-T5-T6 or T5-T6-T7 or T6-T7-T8\n\nT7 only 2 unshown, so T5-T6-T7 possible but T7 scarce.\n\nW5:4 available, so W3-W4-W5 possible.\n\nB1: only 2 left, hard to pair.\n\nHonors: F2 (South), F3 (West), J1 (Red) \u2014 none duplicated.\n\nBest development paths:\n1. Build Character suit: go for W3-W4-W5, then aim for W1-W2-W3 or W6-W7-W8 etc.\n2. Build Bamboo or Dots \u2014 limited.\n3. Keep two T8s for pair, build around T5-T6.\n\nAlso, you have a Chow in Bamboos, so mixed-suit hand likely.\n\nTarget patterns:\n- Mixed Straight: need W123, W456, W789 or similar \u2014 you have W3,W4, could grow\n- All Chows: you have one, can get more\n- Half Flush: if you drop honors, keep only W and T\n- Mixed Shifted Chows: possible\n\nRisks:\n- Holding single honors: easy to discard, but may give points to others\n- F3 is West Wind (Prevalent Wind!) \u2014 very dangerous to discard, as others may have pung\n- F2 is South, not prevalent or seat\n- J1 is Red Dragon \u2014 possible dragon